From ffd211fd10b2e9d7260fb0f5b03b171a679859b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rolotrealanis98 <122947376+rolotrealanis98@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 21:11:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] j716s R1: SMC/battery fixes, macsmc_power.trace, desktop
 bundle (eDP, keyboard backlight, zram, ufw netfilter)

Brings the omarchy-m5 tree level with the R1 integration kernel
(/Volumes/linux-cs/wt-integration, m5pro-linux patches/linux 0016-0033).
Apply after integration 0003.

dt/ (byte-identical to the integration kernel tree's DT sources):
- t6050-smc.dtsi: smc_reboot enabled, apple,poweroff-only, with the
  Abbey PMU scratchpad cells (integration 0017, already verified on
  hardware: clears iBoot's boot-failure counter).
- t6050-jxxx.dtsi: framebuffer0 "apple,internal-panel" -> simpledrm eDP
  connector (Omarchy lid lock, notch-aware bar).
- t6050.dtsi: fpwm0 (disabled); t6050-j716s.dts: fpwm0 enabled +
  pwm-leds "kbd_backlight" (channel 0, 40000 ns, 255 steps).

configs/omarchy-desktop.config (new, merged last): zram+zstd, nf_tables
+ nft_compat + conntrack + xt matches for ufw on iptables-nft,
PWM_APPLE=y, schedutil default, PM_DEBUG/pm_test, hibernation off,
report-only lockup detectors. build-kernel.sh installs and merges it and
checks ZRAM/NF_TABLES/NFT_COMPAT/PWM_APPLE are =y.

patches/linux 0020-0034 (kernel parts only; DT/config hunks live in
dt/ and configs/):
- 0020 RTKit 10 s handshake wait (NVMe ANS), 0021 macsmc-reboot
  poweroff-only;
- 0022-0027 macsmc core: reply-size guard, bounded atomic-write poll,
  key-info lock, key-index bounds, key-count error, optional low-gpio
  cell;
- 0028-0031 macsmc-power: B0RM byte order apart from BCF0 size,
  charge_lock + write reply size, CHLS no forced discharge, optional
  battery properties / TTE-TTF ENODATA;
- 0032 macsmc_power.trace=1 (default off);
- 0033 simpledrm eDP connector for apple,internal-panel;
- 0034 xhci-plat honours wakeup-source (no DT user on J716s yet).

Most SMC/battery and desktop items are based on edimoldovan/linux-aurora
(t6050-j714c: drivers/mfd/macsmc.c, drivers/power/supply/macsmc-power.c,
9dee12b1266c, 9f8535b38fcb, 594f4b3a49ec, 13c28edbabb6); see each kernel
patch for the exact source.

macsmc-power stays gated by initcall_blacklist=macsmc_power_driver_init
in the boot arguments until its test passes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
